**Goal**: prove a cell compiles, runs and reports a result.

**Given**: nothing; this is the smoke test.

**Objectives**

- implement `add_one` so it returns exactly one more than its argument
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §0.1 and §1.1 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: the body can be a single expression with **no** semicolon.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="rust">
/// Return `x` plus one.
///
/// TODO: replace `todo!()` with the incremented value.
fn add_one(x: i32) -> i32 {
    todo!()
}

// --- check (do not modify) ---
assert_eq!(add_one(5), 6);
assert_eq!(add_one(-2), -1);
assert_eq!(add_one(0), 1);
println!("Exercise 0.1 passed");
</VSCode.Cell>
